Cell["\<\
Again, the majority of the fit is coming from case numbers and \
heterozygosity, with less important (but still significant) improvements when \
adding squared case numbers and interactions with heterozygosity.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.956652570941121*^9, 3.956652603363982*^9}, {
  3.9567417808816767`*^9, 3.956741786116729*^9}, {3.965170349898542*^9, 
  3.965170360534893*^9}, {4.001416573810685*^9, 4.001416648650827*^9}, {
  4.001419674294347*^9, 
  4.001419680091724*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"274c7791-a44c-4d9e-b7ab-\
22e449a6971f"],

Cell["\<\
Overall, the linear model fits generally show that both lineage diversity (\
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]expected heterozygosity\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) and \
case numbers are important variables in the model, but the exact functional \
relationship is unclear beyond the linear terms.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.956831912395638*^9, 
  3.95683199601467*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"00dbd786-d80e-4013-87d9-\
d346728882ae"]
}, Closed]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
